<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:folio="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/bpmn"
                  id="Definitions_Process_CodeQualityGates" targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows"
                  exporter="folio-assistant" exporterVersion="1">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_Process_CodeQualityGates">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_Process_CodeQualityGates" name="The gates a change must pass before it can merge" processRef="Process_CodeQualityGates"/>
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_CodeQualityGates" name="The gates a change must pass before it can merge" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>FIVE INDEPENDENT JOBS, AND NOTHING IN THE YAML SAYS SO IN ONE PLACE. Bean `7yvd`. The file is 686 lines and reads as a long sequence; it is not one. No job declares `needs:`, so all five start together and the wall-clock cost of the whole workflow is the SLOWEST job, not the sum. That is the single most useful thing to know before adding a gate, and it is recoverable today only by checking five `needs:` keys that are not there.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;THE ASYMMETRY IS THE OTHER HALF. Four jobs are HARD and one, `rust-wildcard`, carries `continue-on-error: true` &amp;#8212; it reports and cannot block. Drawing them as five equal boxes would be a lie a reader would act on, so the warn-only job is labelled as such and the gateway after the join asks specifically about the HARD ones.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;`continue-on-error` IS NOT A DEFAULT HERE, it is a decision that has been REVERSED once already: `python-imports` carried it, and the flag swallowed a failure on a missing path, so the job reported success over a check that never ran. It was removed and a new unused import now fails. The flag survives on exactly one job, and anyone adding it to a second should read that history first.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;`TypeScript` IS ONE BOX STANDING FOR ROUGHLY THIRTY REPOSITORY GATES &amp;#8212; workflow policy, AGENTS.md cross-references and claims, declared assets, workflow skill refs and BPMN coverage, the knowledge-graph audit, generated-docs currency, agent memory, and the ratchet that fails a check script no workflow runs. They are sequential only because one job runs them; each is independent, and `bun run gates` is the local runner derived from this job so a contributor can run the same set before pushing.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Mechanical throughout. Nothing here waits on a person, which is what makes `build-pipeline` the right lane rather than a convenient one.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <!-- STRICT, and declared (bean `30hn`) — and here the attribute is close
           to a tautology, which is why it is worth writing down rather than
           leaving to the default. The process IS the gate: four hard jobs
           whose failure blocks a merge. A diagram of the gate that was
           advisory about its own steps would be self-contradicting. -->
      <folio:policy enforcement="strict"/>
      <folio:implements workflow=".github/workflows/code-quality-gates.yml"/>
    </bpmn:extensionElements>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_Process_CodeQualityGates">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Ci" name="CI/CD Pipeline">
        <bpmn:documentation>Joins all five jobs before asking anything, then GW_Hard asks specifically about the four HARD ones — Rust's warn-only result reaches the same join but never the gate, so this lane's merge/block call is deliberately blind to a red job it also ran, which is where the five-are-not-four asymmetry actually bites.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_Change</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Fork</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Lean</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Python</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_TypeScript</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_E2E</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Rust</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Join</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Hard</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Pass</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Fail</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_Change" name="Pull request, push to main,&amp;#10;or dispatch">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_0</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:parallelGateway id="GW_Fork" name="All five,&amp;#10;in parallel">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_0</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_2</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_3</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_4</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:parallelGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Lean" name="Lean: no bare&amp;#10;`import Mathlib` (HARD)">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:job name="lean-bare-import"/>
        <folio:skill ref="platform-gates"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Python" name="Python: unused and&amp;#10;wildcard imports (HARD)">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:job name="python-imports"/>
        <folio:skill ref="platform-gates"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_TypeScript" name="TypeScript: tests, lint, types,&amp;#10;and ~30 repository gates (HARD)">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:job name="typescript"/>
        <folio:skill ref="platform-gates"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_8</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_E2E" name="End-to-end +&amp;#10;accessibility (HARD)">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:job name="e2e"/>
        <folio:skill ref="platform-gates"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_9</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Rust" name="Rust wildcard imports&amp;#10;(WARN-ONLY)">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:job name="rust-wildcard"/>
        <folio:skill ref="platform-gates"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_10</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:parallelGateway id="GW_Join" name="">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_7</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_9</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_10</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_11</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:parallelGateway>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Hard" name="Any HARD&amp;#10;gate red?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_11</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_12</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_13</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Pass" name="Mergeable">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_12</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Fail" name="Blocked">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_13</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_0" sourceRef="Start_Change" targetRef="GW_Fork"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1" sourceRef="GW_Fork" targetRef="Task_Lean"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_2" sourceRef="GW_Fork" targetRef="Task_Python"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_3" sourceRef="GW_Fork" targetRef="Task_TypeScript"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_4" sourceRef="GW_Fork" targetRef="Task_E2E"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_5" sourceRef="GW_Fork" targetRef="Task_Rust"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_6" sourceRef="Task_Lean" targetRef="GW_Join"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_7" sourceRef="Task_Python" targetRef="GW_Join"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_8" sourceRef="Task_TypeScript" targetRef="GW_Join"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_9" sourceRef="Task_E2E" targetRef="GW_Join"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_10" sourceRef="Task_Rust" targetRef="GW_Join"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_11" sourceRef="GW_Join" targetRef="GW_Hard"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_12" sourceRef="GW_Hard" targetRef="End_Pass" name="no"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_13" sourceRef="GW_Hard" targetRef="End_Fail" name="yes"/>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_Process_CodeQualityGates">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_Process_CodeQualityGates" bpmnElement="Collaboration_Process_CodeQualityGates">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Participant_Process_CodeQualityGates" bpmnElement="Participant_Process_CodeQualityGates" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="60" y="60" width="1640" height="710"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Ci" bpmnElement="Lane_Ci" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="90" y="60" width="1610" height="600"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Start_Change" bpmnElement="Start_Change">
        <dc:Bounds x="122" y="332" width="36" height="36"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_GW_Fork" bpmnElement="GW_Fork">
        <dc:Bounds x="365" y="325" width="50" height="50"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Lean" bpmnElement="Task_Lean">
        <dc:Bounds x="550" y="70" width="180" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Python" bpmnElement="Task_Python">
        <dc:Bounds x="550" y="190" width="180" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_TypeScript" bpmnElement="Task_TypeScript">
        <dc:Bounds x="550" y="310" width="180" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_E2E" bpmnElement="Task_E2E">
        <dc:Bounds x="550" y="430" width="180" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Rust" bpmnElement="Task_Rust">
        <dc:Bounds x="550" y="550" width="180" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_GW_Join" bpmnElement="GW_Join">
        <dc:Bounds x="865" y="325" width="50" height="50"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_GW_Hard" bpmnElement="GW_Hard">
        <dc:Bounds x="1115" y="325" width="50" height="50"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_End_Pass" bpmnElement="End_Pass">
        <dc:Bounds x="1372" y="332" width="36" height="36"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_End_Fail" bpmnElement="End_Fail">
        <dc:Bounds x="1372" y="452" width="36" height="36"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_0" bpmnElement="Flow_0">
        <di:waypoint x="158" y="350"/>
        <di:waypoint x="365" y="350"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_1" bpmnElement="Flow_1">
        <di:waypoint x="415" y="350"/>
        <di:waypoint x="640" y="350"/>
        <di:waypoint x="640" y="150"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_2" bpmnElement="Flow_2">
        <di:waypoint x="415" y="350"/>
        <di:waypoint x="640" y="350"/>
        <di:waypoint x="640" y="270"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_3" bpmnElement="Flow_3">
        <di:waypoint x="415" y="350"/>
        <di:waypoint x="550" y="350"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_4" bpmnElement="Flow_4">
        <di:waypoint x="415" y="350"/>
        <di:waypoint x="640" y="350"/>
        <di:waypoint x="640" y="430"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_5" bpmnElement="Flow_5">
        <di:waypoint x="415" y="350"/>
        <di:waypoint x="640" y="350"/>
        <di:waypoint x="640" y="550"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_6" bpmnElement="Flow_6">
        <di:waypoint x="730" y="110"/>
        <di:waypoint x="890" y="110"/>
